response:
 The area of a trapezoid is given by the formula \(\frac{1}{2} \times (\text{sum of the bases}) \times \text{height}. Here, one base is \(2x\) and the other base is \(3x\). So, the area \(A\) can be expressed as: \[
A = \frac{1}{2} \times (2x + 3x) \times x = \frac{1}{2} \times 5x \times x = \frac{5x^2}{2}
\]. </think> <answer> \(\frac{5x^2}{2}\) </answer>

